        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Harrison, Paul McCartney, the Beatles\n- Products: Come and Get It: The Best of Apple Records\n- Concepts: Record production, Hinduism, Indian instrumentation\n\nFacts:\n- George Harrison was often referred to as \"the quiet Beatle.\"\n- George Harrison embraced Hinduism.\n- George Harrison helped broaden the horizons of his fellow Beatles and their American audience by incorporating Indian instrumentation into the Beatles' music.\n- On the album Come and Get It: The Best of Apple Records, most recordings were produced by one of the Beatles.\n- On the album Come and Get It: The Best of Apple Records, George Harrison and Paul McCartney were the most heavily represented producers.",
